    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #f7931a;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;">
<p style="color:#9a3412;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 8px;">S5 Q2 — Parse a BIP32 path</p>
<p style="color:#1e293b;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;margin:0;">A path like m/44'/0'/0'/0/0 lists child numbers. A trailing apostrophe means hardened: add 2**31.</p>
</div>
<p style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;">Write <strong><code>parse_path(path)</code></strong> returning the list of integer child numbers. Drop the leading <code>m</code>. For a hardened level (ending in <code>'</code> or <code>h</code>), add <code>2**31</code> to the index.</p>
<div style="background:#fdf4ff;border-left:5px solid #9333ea;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 18px;margin:12px 0;">
<pre style="color:#3b0764;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13px;margin:0;background:none;border:none;">parse_path("m/44'/0'/0'/0/0")
